#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:155
msgid "Building for bare metal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:157
msgid ""
"To build for bare metal, all one has to do is to specify the [system]"
"(https://clang.llvm.org/docs/CrossCompilation.html#target-triple) component "
"of the target triple as `none`. For example, to build for a 32-bit arm "
"target on bare metal, one can use a target triple like `arm-none-eabi`. "
"Other than that, the libc for a bare metal target can be built using any of "
"the three recipes described above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:164
msgid "Building for the GPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:166
msgid ""
"To build for a GPU architecture, it should only be necessary to specify the "
"target triple as one of the supported GPU targets. Currently, this is either "
"`nvptx64-nvidia-cuda` for NVIDIA GPUs or `amdgcn-amd-amdhsa` for AMD GPUs. "
"More detailed information is provided in the {ref}`GPU documentation "
"<libc_gpu_building>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:172
msgid "Building and Testing with an Emulator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:174
msgid ""
"If you are cross-compiling the libc for a different architecture, you can "
"use an emulator such as QEMU to run the tests. For instance, to cross-"
"compile for `riscv64` and run tests using `qemu-riscv64`, you can use the "
"standalone cross build recipe with a few additional CMake flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:180
msgid ""
"Assuming your system compiler (e.g., `clang++`) supports the RISC-V target, "
"you can configure the build as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:201
msgid "The notable additions are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:203
msgid ""
"**The compiler target** - We set `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER_TARGET=riscv64-linux-"
"gnu` and `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_TARGET=riscv64-linux-gnu` to tell CMake to "
"pass the correct `--target` flags to `clang` so that it cross-compiles "
"rather than building for the host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:204
msgid "**The target triple** - We set `-DLIBC_TARGET_TRIPLE=riscv64-linux-gnu`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:205
msgid ""
"**The kernel headers** - We set `-DLIBC_KERNEL_HEADERS=/usr/riscv64-linux-"
"gnu/include` to point to the target's Linux API headers (e.g. for `asm/"
"unistd.h`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:207
msgid ""
"**The cross-compiling emulator** - We set `-"
"DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR=qemu-riscv64` to tell CMake how to execute "
"the compiled unittests. Note that this requires that `qemu-riscv64` is "
"installed and available in your `$PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../full_cross_build.md:210
msgid ""
"**LLD Linker** - We set `-DLLVM_ENABLE_LLD=ON` to ensure the test suite is "
"linked using `lld`, which is necessary for cross-compilation."
msgstr ""

